# Required values must be supplied by the operator; no usable secrets are shipped.
# Export variables or create an ignored local .env; this example itself is not loaded.
# FORMA_IDENTITY_DATABASE_URL (explicit isolated PostgreSQL URL, credentials/port/database required)
# FORMA_AUTH_SECRET (at least 32 random characters; never commit)
# FORMA_ORGANIZATION_ID (explicit child organization)
# FORMA_PUBLIC_ORIGIN (exact loopback Node URL, including its port)
# DATABASE_PATH (explicit owned SQLite path)
# SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_SECURE=true, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASSWORD, SMTP_FROM
API_PORT=8765
PYTHON_BIN=python3
# Authentication profile is fixed password + mandatory TOTP/recovery; providers absent.
